2. Why this term and not a technical measure
--------------------------------------------

An AGPL recipient has the source and may delete any string in it. That is a
freedom the licence grants deliberately, and no technical measure can survive
it — a licence key check in published source is a few minutes' work to remove
and only ever inconveniences the people who would have paid anyway.

Section 7(b) is GPL-compatible and legally enforceable where a technical marking
is neither. So the attribution is held by a licence term rather than by a check
in the binary.

That is the design. It is not yet the build: as of 1 September 2026 the compiled
SDK still carries tier checks from the proprietary model, which an AGPL
recipient is free to remove and which issue #199 removes for everyone. The
obligation in this file is legal either way and does not depend on them.


